# {{TitleName}} — backend (placeholder)

> **Nothing loads this directory.** The backend runtime discovers modules under
> `packages/cli/src/modules/<name>`, where every real backend module lives.
> This is a reserved path for the day frontend and backend halves of a module
> sit side by side — it is not wired to anything today.

To create a backend module that actually runs:

```bash
pnpm setup-backend-module
```

That writes `packages/cli/src/modules/<name>`; see
`scripts/backend-module/backend-module-guide.md`.

Keeping the `id` here identical to the frontend half (`{{name}}`) is what will
make the two sides one module later — both gate off the same
`/rest/module-settings` entry.
